#
# ## fz-kdt.119 re-pricing
#
# `budget.codegen.functions` is `fz.codegen.define_function.stop` from
# `fz2 --emit=stats run <this fixture>`. It moved 35 -> 49 at fz-kdt.119, and
# every one of the fourteen is a `Kernel.dbg/1` or `Kernel.fz_dbg_value/1`
# specialization that BECAME LIVE: the argument's type is a union of
# `{:unknown | any}` at each of three positions, the tuple test used to see
# only "a 3-tuple" and collapsed the eight clauses into one destination, and a
# per-position test tells them apart, so eight arms are minted where one was.
# That 2^arity product is a real cost for a callee that reads no position,
# and fz-kdt.140 owns it.
#
# The number was 29 before this landing and 35 was already the truth, so the
# header was stale by six before anything here touched it. The other nine
# `budget.*` keys on this fixture have no producer anywhere in compiler2 --
# they name a "planner" that does not exist -- and fz-kdt.139 owns removing
# them corpus-wide.
#
# # receive_interleaved_tuple_arity
#
# fz-puj.39 (H14) — matrix-derived shared-constructor verification.
#
# The deleted `same_tuple_arity_run` peephole (fz-puj.23, retired in H12)
# only shared a tuple-arity test across *adjacent* clauses with the same
# arity. The matrix specializer shares across non-adjacent clauses by
# construction: every tuple-3 row, regardless of source position, flows
# into a single `TupleArity = 3` arm; the interleaved atom clause flows
# through the default arm.
#
# Locks behavioral parity (interp / JIT / AOT all consume each message in
# source order) for the adjacency-break shape the old peephole gave up on.
# The shape oracle lives at `ir_lower::tests::receive_oracle_interleaved_tuples_share_via_matrix`.
fn main() do
  send(self(), :ping)
  send(self(), {:warn, 7, 9})
  send(self(), {:msg, 42, 0})

  a = receive do
    {:msg, n, _} -> n
    :ping -> 1
    {:warn, _, t} -> t
  end

  b = receive do
    {:msg, n, _} -> n
    :ping -> 1
    {:warn, _, t} -> t
  end

  c = receive do
    {:msg, n, _} -> n
    :ping -> 1
    {:warn, _, t} -> t
  end

  dbg({a, b, c})
end
